<Project Sdk="Microsoft.NET.Sdk">

  <!--
    Tier 0 - kernel (docs/architecture/modules.md 3).

    Money, Quantity, Percentage, DateRange, strongly-typed id primitives, Result/Error. See
    README.md in this folder for what each type is and the decisions behind it.

    This assembly references nothing but the BCL, and no double or float appears anywhere in it -
    not in a signature, not in a local, not in a cast inside a method body. Do not add a
    PackageReference or a ProjectReference here.

    The mechanism behind both claims is tests/Aurora.Architecture.Tests: rule L1 reads this
    project's declared PackageReference elements and its committed packages.lock.json as well as
    the assembly's emitted references, and rule F1 reads the IL of every method body. B-03 carried
    narrower copies of both in its own test project; B-04 deleted them, because a second rule with
    the same name and a smaller reach is a rule that gets trusted for what it does not do
    (docs/reviews/B-03.md m-1 and m-3).
  -->

  <PropertyGroup>
    <RootNamespace>Aurora.SharedKernel</RootNamespace>
  </PropertyGroup>

</Project>
